  {
   "source": "culturax",
   "order": 3,
   "origin": "hub",
   "repo": "uonlp/CulturaX",
   "revision": "6a8734bc69fefcbb7735f4f9250f43e4cd7a442e",
   "revision_url": "https://huggingface.co/api/datasets/uonlp/CulturaX",
   "config": "vi",
   "gated": true,
   "license_class": "permissive-attribution",
   "note": "Gated on the Hub, auto approved on accepting the terms. The gate is an access control formality rather than a redistribution term, so the class is unchanged, but it has one consequence the manifest has to carry: the Hub masks LFS digests for a gated repo until access is granted, so the digests below are empty and get filled in from the authenticated listing when the grant lands. It is also the number the Vietnamese NLP community treats as the Vietnamese corpus, which is why it is here to be measured against the rest rather than because it is expected to add much.",
   "dropped": true,
   "dropped_because": "Gated, and nobody on this project is in the authorized list. Checked against the live repo on 2026-08-19 rather than against the dataset card: the API answers 200 with gated auto and the pinned revision 6a8734bc69fe is still what main resolves to, and a range request for vi/vi_part_00000.parquet with the ingest token answers 403 GatedRepo, \"Access to dataset uonlp/CulturaX is restricted and you are not in the authorized list\". So this is not a run that failed, it is a person accepting terms, and until somebody does the 50 files and 80.1 GB here cannot be fetched at all. It is dropped rather than left pending because a source that is pinned and not fetched should say so in the one place that lists what the corpus is made of. The cost of leaving it out is smaller than the size suggests: CulturaX is mC4 and OSCAR, both Common Crawl, so it overlaps the four sources that are in the corpus heavily, and the deduplicated union is the number it would move least. The pin stays with its file list so that re-admitting it is one field rather than a re-pin.",
